# Scene flow architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/scene-flow.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/scene-flow.md).

**Permanent decision:** boot scene `game-manager` owns Title → Character Create
→ Home World Select → Starting Hab (and `openSpaceSceneId` / world defaults).
One pure precedence rule (`resolveSceneFlowStep`); Title/Create/Home Select do
not own a competing pipeline. Starting Hab resolves from home world —
[Home Worlds](../../docs/docs/architecture/home-worlds.md). In-play place
changes are markers only — [Game loop](../../docs/docs/architecture/game-loop.md),
[Multiplayer](../../docs/docs/architecture/multiplayer.md). Death respawn is
not this pipeline — [Player death](../../docs/docs/architecture/player-death.md).
Boot / home world picks starting system; Warp Gate changes system during play.

When changing boot, Game Manager hops, `SceneEntryFlow`, home-world entry, or
entry precedence, read the full doc first. Also listed in `AGENTS.md`.
